{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.QBorelResummation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorelResummation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.QHookBound"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qGevrey1_qFactorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qGevrey1_qFactorial","kind":"theorem","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L196-L200","doc":"The q-factorial series `[k]_q!` is q-Gevrey-1 with `C = A = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.summable_qBorel_of_qGevrey1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.summable_qBorel_of_qGevrey1","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L189-L194","doc":"q-Gevrey-1 ⇒ summability of the q-Borel series on the disc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.summable_abs_qBorel_of_qGevrey1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.summable_abs_qBorel_of_qGevrey1","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L178-L187","doc":"**q-Gevrey-1 ⇒ absolute summability** of the q-Borel series on the\ndisc `A·|z| < 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.abs_qBorelCoeff_mul_pow_le_of_qGevrey1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.abs_qBorelCoeff_mul_pow_le_of_qGevrey1","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L166-L176","doc":"Term-wise geometric domination on the disc:\n`|qBorelCoeff q a n · zⁿ| ≤ C · (A·|z|)ⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.abs_qBorelCoeff_le_of_qGevrey1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.abs_qBorelCoeff_le_of_qGevrey1","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L156-L164","doc":"**q-Borel division turns a q-Gevrey-1 bound into a geometric one**:\n`|qBorelCoeff q a n| ≤ C · Aⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.QGevrey1","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.QGevrey1","kind":"def","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L152-L154","doc":"q-Gevrey-1 bound: `|aₙ| ≤ C · Aⁿ · [n]_q!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qBorelCoeff_div_borelCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qBorelCoeff_div_borelCoeff","kind":"theorem","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L133-L143","doc":"**q-Borel to classical Borel ratio.** When `a n ≠ 0`, the ratio of the\nq-Borel coefficient to the classical Borel coefficient is\n`n!/[n]_q!`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qBorelCoeff_eq_borelCoeff_mul_ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qBorelCoeff_eq_borelCoeff_mul_ratio","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L120-L130","doc":"**q-Borel to classical Borel factorization.** The q-Borel coefficient\nequals the classical Borel coefficient times the correction factor\n`n!/[n]_q!`. This is the algebraic identity that the specialization\n`q → 1` sends to `borelCoeff a n * 1 = borelCoeff a n`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.partialQBorel_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.partialQBorel_add","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L100-L107","doc":"The partial q-Borel transform is additive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qBorelCoeff_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qBorelCoeff_smul","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L95-L98","doc":"q-Borel coefficients are homogeneous under scalar multiplication. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qBorelCoeff_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qBorelCoeff_add","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L89-L93","doc":"q-Borel coefficients are additive in the source sequence. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.partialQBorel_qFactorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.partialQBorel_qFactorial","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L78-L85","doc":"The partial q-Borel transform of `Σ [k]_q! zᵏ` is the geometric\npartial sum `Σ_{k=0}^{N} zᵏ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qBorel_tames_qFactorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qBorel_tames_qFactorial","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L70-L76","doc":"**The q-Borel mechanism: division by `[n]_q!` tames q-factorial divergence.**\nThe q-factorial series `Σ [k]_q! zᵏ` has unit q-Borel coefficients.\nThe q-analogue of `borel_tames_factorial`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.partialQBorel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.partialQBorel","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L64-L66","doc":"The partial q-Borel transform: `Σ_{k=0}^{N} (aₖ/[k]_q!) zᵏ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qBorelCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qBorelCoeff","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L59-L62","doc":"The q-Borel transform coefficient: `aₙ / [n]_q!`. Divides by the\nq-factorial instead of `n!`, the q-deformed analogue of `borelCoeff`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qFactReal_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qFactReal_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L52-L55","doc":"`[k]_q! ≠ 0` for `q > 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qFactReal_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.QBorel.qFactReal_pos","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/QBorelResummation.lean#L43-L50","doc":"`[k]_q! > 0` for `q > 1`: the q-factorial is a product of positive\nq-integers. The positivity anchor for the entire q-Borel file. ","signatureChunk":0}]}